 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Planetarium 11 old names to 5 archetypes plus 5; Digistar dropped as a dome-projector system. Astrophotography is new, sourced from AstroBackyard, High Point Scientific and SaaSHub (via firecrawl once). GIS 52 old names trimmed to 4 archetypes plus 8: dropped enterprise servers and libraries (ArcGIS Server, GeoServer, MapServer, PostGIS, OpenLayers, Leaflet, GeoTools, GeoTrellis, GeoNetwork, MapDotNet, Oracle Spatial, GeoMedia and WebMap, SuperMap, Smallworld, TNTmips, TerraLib, TerraView), transport modelling (TransModeler), fleet (GeoBase) and ETL (FME). Scientific software cut from 142 to 7 archetypes plus 17; dropped trade/niche/dead: Alteryx, BMDP, S-PLUS, Statistica, RATS, LIMDEP, NLOGIT, Shazam, TSP, Ox, XploRe, ELKI, PRIMER, ADMB, AMPL, COMSOL, LabVIEW, OpenFOAM, Trilinos, libraries (LAPACK, ScaLAPACK, Armadillo, NumPy, pandas, SciPy, scikit-learn, Torch, mlpack) and others. GeoGebra is named in the brief but no retrieved page covered it, so it is omitted."
}